  "body": "For those drawn to life on the water, this is a home with a genuine point of difference.\r\n\r\nPositioned along Takapuna's coveted Golden Mile, this vibrant two-bedroom residence enjoys direct access to Lake Pupuke, while Milford Beach is just a few minutes' walk in the opposite direction. Morning swims, paddleboarding from the lake edge, sunset walks along the beach - here, the water becomes part of everyday life.\r\n\r\nInside, the home is light, warm and full of personality. Soaring angled ceilings, skylights and an abundance of natural light give the open-plan living spaces an uplifting sense of volume, while the contemporary kitchen connects effortlessly with the living and dining zones. Relaxed yet considered, this is a home with genuine character and soul.\r\n\r\nTwo generous double bedrooms offer excellent wardrobe space, complemented by a beautifully renovated bathroom with a bath and separate WC. Double glazing and a heat pump enhance year-round comfort, while the low-maintenance nature of the property makes it an ideal lock-and-leave for those who value freedom without compromising on style.\r\n\r\nThen there is the location. Lake access is quite literally at your doorstep, Milford Beach is moments away, and both Milford and Takapuna offer an exceptional selection of cafes, restaurants, boutiques and everyday amenities within easy reach.\r\n\r\nFor city commuters, the connection is equally effortless, with the 82 bus stopping only metres from home and providing a direct route into the CBD.\r\n\r\nIndividual, energetic and wonderfully connected, this is a home for someone who values lifestyle - a distinctive retreat between the lake and the sea, with all the ease of lock-and-leave living.\r\n\r\nAUCTION: 2:00pm, Thursday 22 October 2026, at 3 Pompallier Terrace, Ponsonby (Unless Sold Prior).",
